    "why_it_is_not_one": "The check fires when the repeats disagree, so it misses when every fit lands on the same branch. A previous version of this record explained the residual as the branches agreeing by chance, following (1-p)^n + p^n. That explanation is withdrawn: see independence_of_the_fits, which tests it against the per-fit split measured in the same process and finds it does not hold. The rates above are measurements and are not derived from any model.",
    "independence_of_the_fits": {
      "model_tested": "(1-p)^n + p^n, for n fits and a fixed per-fit minority p",
      "per_fit_minority_rate_measured_in_this_process": 0.25,
      "exponent_is": "the number of fits, which is one plus the repeats",
      "predictions": [
        {
          "fits": 5,
          "probability_all_fits_agree": 0.238281,
          "predicted_misses": 7.148,
          "observed_misses": 5,
          "one_sided_p_of_at_most_the_observed": 0.2464
        },
        {
